{%- comment -%}
ART AVENUE - PRODUCT BUILD CHECKLIST
Reference only. Never rendered. Sits alongside aa-chair-schema-templates and
aa-storage-schema-templates.

WHY THIS EXISTS
A configurator product depends on THREE metafields working together. Miss any
one and the PDP degrades SILENTLY - no error, no warning, no console message.
The option simply does not appear, and it looks like a theme bug rather than
missing data. Every gap listed below was shipped live at least once.

================================================================
1. THE THREE METAFIELDS - all required, all fail silently
================================================================

aav.configurator        json
  The schema: engine, size_option, material_option, unit_map, tier_filters,
  pickers. WITHOUT IT: no configurator renders at all (loudest failure - you
  will notice this one).

aav.swatches            list.metaobject_reference
  The POOL that tier_filters and pickers draw from. Filters only FILTER this
  list - they do NOT query the global swatch library.
  WITHOUT IT: every picker vanishes. No error.
  MISMATCHED: a filter naming a category absent from the list yields zero
  swatches and the picker vanishes just the same. Changing a tier_filter
  category ALWAYS means changing this list too. Never one without the other.

aav.size_dimensions     json
  Per-size dual units: { "One Size": { "cm": "...", "in": "..." } }
  Keys MUST match the Size option values exactly.
  WITHOUT IT: falls back to configurator unit_map - cm only, no inches.

Also set, where the family uses them:
  aav.wood_finishes     list.metaobject_reference  (any picker with
                        source: "wood_finishes" - offer the full set, not one)
  aav.short_description multi_line_text_field      (see section 3)
  aav.dim_w / dim_d / dim_h   number_integer

================================================================
2. SWATCH LIBRARIES - pick the right one
================================================================

"Leather"            upholstery - sofas, chairs, bed headboards
"Furniture Leather"  trunks, chests, wardrobes, cabinets, tables
"Table Leather"      table tops
"Storage Hardware"   Antique Brass / Silver / Gold
"Legs"               Wooden Legs / Metal Legs
"Handle"             Leather Handles / Metal Knobs / Metal Handles
"Leg Wood"           Natural Oak / Walnut / Blackwood
"Leg Metal"          Antique Brass / Matte Black / Brushed Nickel

Beds sit on "Leather" DELIBERATELY - the headboard is upholstery, not a
wrapped carcass. This is not drift. Do not "fix" it.

Kilim trim uses "Furniture Leather" restricted to Saddle and Onyx.
(Formerly Chestnut and Ebony on "Leather" - remapped 2026-08-22.)

Ebony = leather colour. Blackwood = wood finish. Keep them distinct.

================================================================
3. COPY
================================================================

short_description  Complete sentences. This is the blurb under the price.
                   Without it the theme truncates the description at 28 words,
                   which cuts mid-sentence on any long description.
description        Required. Five products shipped live with this EMPTY.

NEVER claim "full-grain leather" anywhere. This has resurfaced twice after
being swept. Grep before every launch.

Size nomenclature by category:
  sofas - seater count | rectangular coffee tables - Compact / Grand
  round tables - diameter in cm | rugs - ft with cm sublabels

================================================================
4. VARIANTS
================================================================

inventoryPolicy: CONTINUE on every variant (made-to-order: a variant
existing means it is orderable).
inventoryPolicy DENY is INERT on untracked variants - Shopify treats
untracked as infinitely available. Set inventoryItem.tracked = true too,
if you ever actually need DENY.

Prices are GST-INCLUSIVE (shop.taxesIncluded = true). A quoted ex-GST cost
MUST be grossed up before entry. Check the number against sibling products -
an odd figure beside round ones is usually an un-grossed cost price.

Check for cannibalisation: a product must not undercut a sibling that offers
less. Compare against the whole family before publishing.

================================================================
5. MERCHANDISING
================================================================

Smart collections match on EXACT tag strings. "Chest of Drawers" does NOT
match a collection ruled on "chests-of-drawers" - that shipped as an empty
live collection linked from the main menu. Add the hyphenated tag AND
verify productsCount afterwards.

publishablePublish is a SEPARATE call after productSet and collectionCreate.
Neither publishes automatically.

Photos: hero first (clean 3/4 of the object), then front, then detail, then
lifestyle. Never lead a made-to-order configurator with a lifestyle shot.

================================================================
6. VERIFY BEFORE CALLING IT DONE
================================================================

[ ] Load the PDP. Every picker renders with more than one option.
[ ] Dimensions box shows BOTH cm and inches.
[ ] Size hint (top right) shows a value - "One Size" included.
[ ] Blurb under the price is a complete sentence, no ellipsis.
[ ] Description body is not empty.
[ ] Price is GST-inclusive and consistent with its family.
[ ] Product appears in every intended collection (check counts, not rules).
[ ] Product and collections are published to Online Store.

Theme edits: themeFilesUpsert replaces the WHOLE file. Always re-query
size + checksumMd5 afterwards to confirm no truncation. themeFilesDelete
is blocked via the API - removal goes through git rm.
